J.5 Denoising Diffusion Policy

Forward diffusion (noise injection, fixed schedule):

```
 a^0        a^1        a^2               a^K
  ●─────●─────●───── ... ─────●
  clean     + noise                pure noise ~ N(0,I)
  q(a^k|a^{k-1}) = N(√(1-β_k) a^{k-1}, β_k I)
```

Reverse process (learned denoising, conditioned on observation o):

```
 a^K        a^{K-1}        a^{K-2}       ...        a^0
  ●─────●─────●───── ... ─────●
  noise    ←  μ_θ(a^k, o, k)                 predicted action sequence
  p_θ(a^{k-1}|a^k, o) = N(μ_θ, σ_k^2 I)
  μ_θ parameterised via noise prediction: ε_θ(a^k, o, k)
```

Training minimises the simple loss: E ||ε – ε_θ(a^k, o, k)||².

